multiple-choice questions for https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B

    llm.decide(state, "did the deployment succeed?", ["yes", "no", "unclear"])
    -> {"yes": 0.91, "no": 0.03, "unclear": 0.06}

a language model writes one token per forward pass. but after the
first pass it already holds a score for every possible next token,
including A, B and C. those scores are the answer. this reads them
and stops.

    chat       generate "yes" token by token, parse it.  one sample.
    readout    one pass, softmax over A B C.             the whole distribution.

a grammar only filters what chat may generate. it is still chat.

the model cannot think before a one-token answer. for anything
that needs reasoning, or output longer than a choice, use chat.

https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev did this with a 4B model.

quick demo:

    $ ./run.sh uv run example.py
